BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:the-start-of-ramadan-20270208@todaycelebrates.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270208
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270209
SUMMARY:The Start of Ramadan
DESCRIPTION:Ramadan is the ninth month of the Islamic lunar calendar and th
 e month in which observant Muslims fast from dawn to sunset\, one of the f
 ive Pillars of Islam. Its first day is not a fixed date but a determinatio
 n\, made fresh each year from a crescent moon that different authorities r
 ead in different ways — which is why mosques in the same American city s
 ometimes begin on different days. Because the lunar year runs about eleven
  days shorter than the solar one\, it moves backward through the seasons\,
  returning to where it started roughly every thirty-three years.\n\nhttps:
 //todaycelebrates.com/holiday/the-start-of-ramadan/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/the-start-of-ramadan/
CATEGORIES:Community
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
